SELinux generation tracking regression
The issue originates from upstream commit c70c717, which introduced SELinux policy generation tracking for policy updates.
However, this commit introduced compatibility issues in rules.c, particularly with the reset_avc_cache() implementation and policy generation handling.
The follow-up commit 6076949 addresses the regression by correcting the AVC cache reset calls for older kernels.
Note: The seqno0 typo and policydb->latest_granting reference in my current source also need correction. These are additional source-level mistakes that must be fixed before the build can proceed.
